From: pocket-debs <masterxq@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mobileshell: status bar: one indicator per connection, states of activation and failure
Description:
 The internet indicator showed the icon of the primary connection and,
 while any connection was being activated (mobile data included), a busy
 indicator in its place. With Wi-Fi connected and mobile data activating,
 the Wi-Fi icon turned into a spinner that told nothing about the
 connection it stood for.
 .
 The status bar now has a fixed indicator per connection, each shown only
 when it matters: the signal of every SIM; the Wi-Fi signal while Wi-Fi is
 connected or connecting; the hotspot while it is active; the airplane
 icon in place of the signals in airplane mode. There is no generic
 internet icon and no busy indicator; wired and USB connections have no
 indicator. The icons are the ones the connection icon of plasma-nm
 names: network-mobile-<strength>-<type> with the letter of the network
 type for the SIM with mobile data, network-wireless-<strength> for Wi-Fi,
 with the -locked (VPN) and -limited (limited connectivity) variants on
 the icon of the primary connection.
 .
 While mobile data is being activated only the letter of the network type
 pulses (the part of the icon with the letter, over the icon without
 it); the Wi-Fi icon pulses as a whole. After a minute the pulsing part
 turns to the negative color (still trying, not working yet). After a
 failed activation a red cross of the size of the letter takes its place,
 or sits at the bottom right of the Wi-Fi icon, until the connection is up
 or the user disables and enables mobile data or Wi-Fi; retries of
 NetworkManager do not bring the pulsing back. Without a known network
 type three dots stand in the letter area; for EDGE, whose Breeze icons
 have no letter, an E is drawn. Nothing changes its size between states.
 .
 Pulsing: opacity from invisible to visible, 1 s fade in, 0.2 s visible,
 1 s fade out, 0.2 s invisible, sine easing, one phase for all indicators
 (IndicatorPulse). The opacity changes in steps (8 per second during the
 fades, none during the holds) instead of an animation at the frame rate,
 so the status bar is redrawn about 7 times per second while something
 pulses. The pulse runs only while a screen is on (DPMS); with animations
 disabled the pulsing part is shown half transparent.
 .
 Needs the plasma-nm libraries with WirelessStatus.wifiState/
 wifiSignalStrength, ConnectionIcon.vpn/limited and
 CellularModem.mobileDataState.
Forwarded: no
License: GPL-2.0-or-later, LGPL-2.0-or-later (as the patched files; new files GPL-2.0-or-later)
Last-Update: 2026-11-26
